version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Gnomon voice (docs/specs/gnomon.md §14; the spec node #gnomon-voice is the
  kernel-supervised voice child and is not built yet). This directory holds
  its first native piece, the darwin audio I/O binary (TD-2026-10-19-298,
  slice V2b, T-2026-10-19-026): io-darwin/ is a SwiftPM package (swift-tools
  5.9, macOS 14), scripts/build-voice-io.mjs bundles and signs it as
  GnomonVoiceIO.app (bin/, gitignored; checksums.json after a signed build).
  PROBES.md holds the founder's P1 (TCC attribution) and P7 (AEC leak) steps.
  macOS only: CI builds and tests it on the macOS runner of the native job,
  never on Windows or Linux.

components:
  gnomon-voice:
    description: >-
      The voice client core in Node, @a-company/gnomon-voice (spec §14, slice
      V2c, TD-2026-10-19-298, T-2026-10-19-026). It connects as the talk-only
      voice principal p:<ns>/voice with keys/voice.key, reads the attachment
      and the human's ceiling from status.voice, and runs modes OFF, PTT and
      AMBIENT (it may narrow the mode locally, never widen it). Engines come
      from sherpa-onnx-node 1.13.8, an optional native dependency: Silero VAD,
      Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 int8, Kokoro-82M int8 en and 3D-Speaker CAM++
      speaker embeddings. Every engine is injected through the AudioIO,
      VadEngine, SttEngine, TtsEngine, SpeakerEngine and KernelLink
      interfaces. SpawnedAudioIO speaks gnomon-voice-io:v1 to the V2b binary.
      It refuses to capture when the binary is not disclaimed, drops frames
      after mic off, spawns the binary with a clean env, and takes the aec
      claim and the transport from the route event. FakeAudioIO plays WAV
      fixtures. voice-models.manifest.json pins each model's URL, sha256 and
      size; `models fetch` verifies every download (0700) and refuses one
      that does not match, and every model file is re-hashed before it is
      loaded. Prints are embeddings only, stored in voice/prints/<name>/.
      Audio is never written to disk (G-VOX-05).
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, client, paradigm-8, v2c]
    flows: [$voice-turn]
  gnomon-voice-io:
    description: >-
      The voice child's audio I/O, mic only (no keychain group, no network,
      writes only stdout/stderr). Protocol gnomon-voice-io:v1, the same
      framing both ways: type:u8 length:u32le payload (max 1 MiB); 0x01 JSON
      (stdin commands, stdout replies and events), 0x02 capture (stdout:
      hostTimeNs:u64le sampleRate:u32le s16le, 16 kHz mono after voice
      processing), 0x03 playback (stdin: sampleRate:u32le s16le mono TTS,
      8-48 kHz). Commands info, mic.on, mic.off, play.stop (barge-in flush),
      play.end, route.get, hotkeys.set {bindings}, quit; each gets one reply
      {type:'reply', id, op, ok}. Events (tUs monotonic µs, the capture
      clock): ready, mic, route {route, aec: vpio|headphones|none}, level
      {rmsDBFS, peakDBFS} ~15 Hz, playback.start {audibleAtUs},
      playback.end {reason: drained|stopped|mic-switch|route-change|exit},
      hotkey {action: talk|mic-toggle|mode-toggle, phase: down|up}, engine,
      error, exit. Mic on = one AVAudioEngine with
      inputNode.setVoiceProcessingEnabled(true) (VoiceProcessingIO AEC) and
      a player node in the same engine, so TTS is the echo reference; mic
      off stops and releases that engine (no orange dot) and TTS plays via an
      output-only engine that never touches inputNode. Route from CoreAudio
      (default output device transport + built-in data source, listeners
      on both). Hotkeys via Carbon RegisterEventHotKey, press and release,
      no Input Monitoring; defaults ctrl+alt+space (talk), ctrl+alt+m,
      ctrl+alt+a; reported only, the controller acts. Mic modes re-spawn
      with TCC responsibility disclaimed so the Microphone grant names
      GnomonVoiceIO (probe P1; --no-disclaim is the control). --version,
      --selftest (1 s smoke), --probe-aec <file> (P7); stdin EOF exits 0.
      VoiceIOCore (frame codec, command parser, hotkey config, level and
      route math) is pure and covered by swift test (26 XCTests).
    path: io-darwin/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, native, swift, paradigm-8, audio, v2b]
  gnomon-voice-io-build:
    description: >-
      scripts/build-voice-io.mjs: swift build -c release → GnomonVoiceIO.app
      (bundle id gnomon.voice-io, LSUIElement, NSMicrophoneUsageDescription
      "Gnomon voice listens only while the mic is on."), codesign
      --options runtime --timestamp with the one Developer ID Application
      identity of team SW4BMQ8PNL (looked up via the helper's signing.mjs),
      exactly one entitlement com.apple.security.device.audio-input, no
      provisioning profile and no keychain group; verifies --strict, the
      VOICE_IO_REQUIREMENT, the entitlement set and the runtime flag; sha256
      into checksums.json (advisory). --unsigned for CI. No notarization
      (founder-run).
    path: scripts/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, signing, build, v2b]

flows:
  voice-turn:
    description: >-
      One spoken turn (spec §14.2). User side: AudioIO frames, then the PTT
      held span or a VAD segment, then the gates (attached, mode within the
      ceiling, outside every playback window plus 750 ms), then STT, then
      speaker verification, then log.append voice.turn.user{turnId,
      speakerId, speakerEnrolled, forwarded, mode, aec, aecTransport, t0,
      t1, text}, then session.send content [{text}] for enrolled speakers
      only. Unknown speakers are logged with no text. A refusal is shown
      and never retried. Agent side: log.read follow, then the speakable
      summary (the gnome line or the first paragraph; edits are said as
      "edited N files"; ask-user questions are always read), then Kokoro
      one sentence at a time, then play, then voice.turn.agent{t0, t1,
      textPlanned, textSpoken}. Barge-in: 300 ms of speech, or the talk key,
      stops playback and drops the rest of the reply.
    steps: ["#gnomon-voice", "#gnomon-voice-io"]

